Description: screenshot and image markup tools for Linux Mint
 xl-Screenshot takes a screenshot of the whole screen, a single window, or
 a selection you draw, with an optional delay. The capture can be copied,
 saved as PNG, JPEG or WebP, or marked up in xl-Annotate. An optional tray
 icon starts a selection with one click.
 .
 xl-Annotate adds arrows, lines, freehand drawing, rectangles, ellipses,
 highlights, text, numbered steps, pixelation, a magnifying loupe and
 cropping to any image. Rough freehand shapes are tidied into clean ones,
 and marks stay editable until the image is saved. It also appears as
 "Annotate Image…" in Nemo's right-click menu.
